      "readTimeSeconds": 75,
      "tags": ["Tech", "App", "Excuses", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "160",
      "headline": "Tech Company Creates 'Honest GPS' That Shows Real-Time Regret About Your Life Choices",
      "summary": "The 'LifeRegret Navigator' calculates your route based on 'all the wrong turns you've made to get here.'",
      "fullBody": "HonestNavigation Corp has created 'LifeRegret Navigator,' a GPS system that shows you in real-time all the wrong turns you've made in life. Instead of showing optimal routes, the system displays 'You could have taken a different career path here' and 'This exit leads to the job you actually wanted but you chose comfort instead.' One user said, 'I was driving to work and the GPS said "If you'd taken that job in 2019, you'd be driving a better car right now. Turn left into regret." I had to pull over.' The system also has a 'future projection' feature that shows where your current path leads, which users report is 'depressing but accurate.' The company is working on a 'Life Do-Over Mode' but hasn't figured out how to make that work yet.",
      "category": "tech",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/160.jpg",
      "imagePrompt": "GPS screen showing route with wrong turns labeled REGRET TURN, person driving looking sad, speech bubble from GPS saying IF YOU'D MADE DIFFERENT CHOICES, comic illustration, flat design, gray and red colors",
      "publishedAt": "10 hrs ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 80,
      "tags": ["Tech", "GPS", "Regret", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "161",
      "headline": "Man Creates 'Auto-Compliment Machine' That Compliments Him Constantly To Boost Self-Esteem",
      "summary": "The 'GaryValidation' system has 47 pre-recorded compliments that play on loop whenever he walks by.",
      "fullBody": "Self-esteem entrepreneur Gary Needier has created the 'GaryValidation' system, a series of speakers installed around his home and office that automatically play compliments when he walks by. The system has 47 pre-recorded compliments like 'You look great today,' 'That was a good decision,' and 'You're doing better than you think.' One installer said, 'I programmed the system to compliment him every time he enters a room, and he literally stood in the doorway for 47 minutes getting compliments. He was crying happy tears.' Gary says the system has 'changed his life' and he's 'never felt more validated.' His wife says, 'He used to need other people's approval, now he needs a machine's approval, so I guess we've made progress?' The system is available for pre-order.",
      "category": "tech",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/161.jpg",
      "imagePrompt": "Man walking through house while speakers automatically play YOU LOOK GREAT TODAY, man crying happy tears, wife looking concerned, comic illustration, flat design, purple and gray colors",
      "publishedAt": "11 hrs ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 77,
      "tags": ["Tech", "Self-Esteem", "Compliments", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "162",
      "headline": "New AI 'Reality Check Bot' Sends You Messages When You're Being Unreasonable",
      "summary": "The 'GaryReality' AI responds to your texts with 'That's not how any of this works, let me explain.'",
      "fullBody": "Honest Communication Technologies has released 'GaryReality,' an AI that sends you reality check messages whenever you're being unreasonable, dramatic, or just wrong. The AI monitors your texts and interjects with messages like 'You're not being persecuted, you're just being asked to do your job' and 'That person didn't wrong you, they just didn't prioritize you, which is different.' One user said, 'I was about to send a angry text about how my friend 'never' texts me back, and GaryReality sent 'Actually, they text you back more than you text them. You're the problem here.' I almost threw my phone.' The AI has been credited with 'saving relationships' and 'ruining the satisfaction of being dramatic.' A premium version offers 'in-person reality checks via phone call.'",
      "category": "tech",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/162.jpg",
