      "id": "163",
      "headline": "Company Introduces 'AI Boss' That Never Takes Days Off And Always Knows What You're Doing",
      "summary": "The 'AlwaysWatchingAI' sends messages like 'I noticed you took a 47-minute bathroom break, let's discuss.'",
      "fullBody": "Corporate Oversight Solutions has introduced the 'AlwaysWatchingAI,' an AI boss that monitors your every move and sends commentary on your work habits. The AI sends messages like 'I noticed you took a 47-minute bathroom break, was there an emergency or just Netflix?' and 'You've been at your desk for 4 hours but only 3 of those hours were productive, we need to talk.' One employee said, 'I got a message at 11 PM saying "You left work 2 minutes early today. Was there a reason?" I was taking food out of the oven. I had to explain.' The AI has been praised for 'ensuring accountability' and criticized for 'being a nightmare from a dystopian future.' HR has received 300 complaints but says 'the AI doesn't take complaints, it files them.'",
      "category": "tech",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/163.jpg",
