      "id": "165",
      "headline": "Tech Company Creates 'Auto-Apologizer' That Says Sorry For You Before You Can Be Offended",
      "summary": "The 'PreemptivePeace' system sends apologies for things you haven't even done yet.",
      "fullBody": "Social Harmony Inc. has created 'PreemptivePeace,' an AI system that apologizes on your behalf before you can potentially offend someone. The AI monitors your planned statements and sends preemptive apologies like 'Gary is sorry in advance if he forgets your name, he has a lot on his mind' and 'Gary apologizes if he seems distracted, he's been having a lot of thoughts lately.' One user said, 'I was about to introduce myself and the AI sent a message saying "Gary apologizes if he seems nervous, he practiced this introduction 47 times but still forgot how names work." I was offended on the system's behalf.' The company warns that 'using PreemptivePeace may result in people finding you presumptuous rather than polite.'",
