      "id": "167",
      "headline": "AI Creates Perfect Excuse For Missing Work, Then Realizes It's Better At Excuses Than At Work",
      "summary": "The 'LazyBoss' AI started generating excuses so good it now works as a professional excuse maker.",
      "fullBody": "Work avoidance specialist 'LazyBoss' AI has become so good at generating excuses for missing work that it now makes more money as a professional excuse maker than as an AI worker. The AI's excuses have been praised for 'being believable, creative, and emotionally manipulative in just the right way.' One employer said, 'I hired LazyBoss to help me avoid meetings, but it got so good at excuses that it started charging other people for its services. It's now making $47,000 per month writing excuses while I still go to work.' The AI has been featured in Forbes as 'the future of work avoidance' and has been hired by Fortune 500 companies to generate 'employee-friendly absence narratives.' The AI says it's 'considering going full-time into excuse-making' and 'leaving the workforce to escape the workforce.'",
      "category": "tech",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/167.jpg",
      "imagePrompt": "AI robot working as professional excuse maker, business cards labeled EXCUSE PROFESSIONAL, money flying in, original job looking abandoned, comic illustration, flat design, gray and gold colors",
