      "id": "169",
      "headline": "Company Releases 'Honest Calendar' That Only Shows Events You're Actually Going To Attend",
      "summary": "The 'RealSchedule' system removes events you've missed 47 times and calls it 'digital minimalism.'",
      "fullBody": "FinallyRealistic Corp has released 'RealSchedule,' a calendar app that only shows events you're actually going to attend, removing everything you've missed or avoided. The app sends daily notifications like 'This meeting has been on your calendar for 47 days and you've avoided it for 47 days straight, we're removing it for your own good.' One user said, 'I used to have 47 events per week, now I have 3, and I've actually gone to all of them because they're the only ones that matter. My stress levels dropped 90%.' The app also has a 'someday maybe' folder for events you keep rescheduling, which the app calls 'the graveyard of good intentions.' The company reports that users are 'happier but less busy' which they consider 'a win.'",
      "category": "tech",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/169.jpg",
      "imagePrompt": "Calendar showing 47 events being deleted down to 3, person looking relieved, ghost events being removed to GRAVEYARD, comic illustration, flat design, green and gray colors",
