    {
      "id": "174",
      "headline": "New Service 'Professional Nag' Texts You Reminders Every 47 Minutes Until You Do Things",
      "summary": "The 'GaryReminder' service never stops until your task is complete, then moves to the next one.",
      "fullBody": "FinallyGetting Things Done Inc. has released 'Professional Nag,' a service that texts you reminders every 47 minutes until you complete your tasks. The system sends messages like 'Did you do the thing yet? No? Why not? I'm asking because I care but also because I'm programmed to annoy you.' and 'This is your 47th reminder about the thing. At this point, the thing is judging you. Do the thing.' One user said, 'I had a task I'd been avoiding for 47 days. I hired Professional Nag and within 3 days I'd completed it because I couldn't handle the texts anymore. It was effective and also psychological torture.' The service is subscription-based at $47 per month and includes 'nag packages' for different personality types.",
      "category": "lifestyle",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/174.jpg",
      "imagePrompt": "Person receiving 47th text saying DID YOU DO THE THING YET, phone buzzing constantly, task sitting undone looking scared, comic illustration, flat design, gray and red colors",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 75,
      "tags": ["Lifestyle", "Reminders", "Services", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "175",
      "headline": "Man Creates 'Automatic Motivation Machine' That Plays Speech Clips Whenever He Tries To Quit",
      "summary": "The 'GaryMotivation' system activates whenever he tries to give up, playing 'You can do this!' on loop.",
      "fullBody": "Self-improvement enthusiast Gary Motivated has created the 'GaryMotivation' machine, a device that plays motivational speeches whenever he tries to quit something. The system activates through motion sensors and delivers messages like 'You can do this!' 'Don't give up now!' and 'You're stronger than you think!' on loop for as long as Gary attempts to stop. One session lasted 47 hours when Gary tried to quit learning piano. Gary said, 'I was ready to give up after 10 minutes but the machine kept saying 'You've practiced for 10 minutes, don't waste it now!' I cried, but I also learned to play chopsticks.' The machine has been credited with 'making Gary finish things' and criticized for 'being the motivational speaker equivalent of a persistent蚊.'",
      "category": "lifestyle",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/175.jpg",
      "imagePrompt": "Person trying to quit piano, motivational speaker machine playing YOU CAN DO THIS on loop, person crying but practicing, comic illustration, flat design, purple and gray colors",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 78,
      "tags": ["Lifestyle", "Motivation", "Machine", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "176",
      "headline": "New Hair Salon Offers 'Brutally Honest Mirror' That Comments On Your Hair Choices",
      "summary": "The 'Truth Mirror' says things like 'Are you sure about this cut? I'm asking for science.'",
      "fullBody": "The Brutal Beauty salon has installed a 'Truth Mirror' in every styling station that provides unfiltered commentary on customers' hair decisions. The mirror uses AI to analyze cuts and colors and delivers honest feedback like 'This color makes you look like you're going through a phase' and 'That cut is fine, but you could do better, we've both seen your previous styles.' One customer said, 'I showed the mirror a photo of a style I wanted and it said 'That's a lot of commitment for something that will look bad in 3 weeks, but you do you.' I cried, but my hair does look better now.' The salon reports a 47% increase in customers who 'want someone to tell them the truth about their hair.' The mirror also offers complimentary insults about outfit choices.",
      "category": "lifestyle",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-10/176.jpg",
      "imagePrompt": "Person in salon chair looking in mirror that has angry face and speech bubble saying THAT'S A CHOICE, stylist in background shrugging, comic illustration, flat design, pink and gray colors",
      "publishedAt": "1 day ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 78,
      "tags": ["Lifestyle", "Salon", "Mirror", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
