      "headline": "Scientists Confirm That 'I'm Not Jealous' Means 'I Am Extremely Jealous And This Is A Defense Mechanism'",
      "summary": "The study found that 'not jealous' correlates 100% with 'just saw your promotion on LinkedIn.'",
      "fullBody": "Emotional researchers at the Institute of Questionable Feelings have confirmed that 'I'm not jealous' means 'I am extremely jealous and this is a defense mechanism.' The study found that people who say 'I'm not jealous' often send a text immediately after seeing their ex's vacation photos, their coworker's promotion, or their friend's new relationship. One participant said, 'I'm definitely not jealous that you got promoted, I'm so happy for you, really.' Researchers observed that the 'really' at the end of that sentence was the tell. The study found that 'not jealous' is often followed by 'but how did you get that before me?' which proves the point. Researchers recommend 'just admitting you're jealous because it's a normal human emotion' but note that 'pride prevents this 100% of the time.'",
