      "headline": "New App 'Mood Tracker' That Only Records Negative Emotions, Calls It 'Realistic Mental Health'",
      "summary": "The 'HonestMind' app deletes all positive entries because 'happiness is just denial with a smile.'",
      "fullBody": "Anti-Sugarcoating Mental Health Technologies has released 'HonestMind,' a mood tracking app that only records negative emotions and deletes anything positive because 'happiness is just denial with a smile.' The app sends weekly reports showing 'Your week was mostly terrible with occasional moments of not being terrible, here's the breakdown.' One user said, 'I tried to log 'feeling good' and the app said 'That's not a real emotion, try again with something authentic.' I logged 'mildly okay' instead.' The app has been praised for 'finally being honest about mental health' and criticized by therapists who say 'we need to track the good things too.' The company responds with 'the good things don't need tracking, they need to be questioned.'",
