      "headline": "Company Introduces 'Boss For A Day' Service Where Strangers Manage Your Life",
      "summary": "The 'Accountability Partners Inc.' assigns someone to tell you what to do for $47 per hour.",
      "fullBody": "FinallyResponsible Corp has introduced 'Boss For A Day,' a service that assigns you a stranger to manage your life for a day. The 'boss' shows up at your house and tells you what to do, like 'You're going to the gym now, no arguments,' 'You're eating a salad, I don't care if you don't like salad,' and 'You're going to bed at a reasonable hour, your health is my problem now.' One customer said, 'I hired a boss for a day and she made me clean my entire apartment, organize my closet, and have a difficult conversation with my mother. It was terrible and I lost 5 pounds from the stress. I feel great.' The service is fully booked for the next 47 months with a waiting list of people who 'need someone to make them do things.'",
